so Peter we recently got to take a look  at a game that's very much in the  minecraft style sort of game with a  little bit of building a little bit of  shooting a little bit of teamwork and  it's called block and load yeah jagex is  blocking load is a sort of unapologetic  game is inspired by minecraft and you  know yes it's a competitive shooter it's  team-based and the way it divides the  gameplay up is before any match starts  you literally take five minutes to  harvest resources and build things on  your team's base because so there's a  generator that you're trying to throw  behind enemy lines so it's your job to  protect yours and sort of build  fortification around it you know perhaps  so the enemy has to dig through that to  get to your generator yeah so it's  interesting that they have the the setup  period before the actual shooting begins  because it you know in traditional  minecraft style it front loads each  match with sort of a building period  where you can just sort of get creative  and you know dig a hole dig a bunker  someone on our team during the demo  built a pill box with a bunch of turrets  in there so you can get really creative  on how you want to defend your generator  before you even have to worry about  finding the other teams right and so  after the building phase the match  starts and you know teams are comprised  of different classes of characters and  as some of these characters include a  rainbow look like a sort of a tank like  giant robot and he's even a quick little  ninja type character and yeah i mean  everyone kind of runs for the generator  but ultimately you die pretty quickly in  this game if your enemies set up turrets  or if they're good at attacking you but  there's a way to sort of alleviate that  you know that punishment for going back  yeah so it's possible to build sort of  similar to the tf2 engineers teleporters  you can build spawn points throughout  the map so it's interesting because you  can dig down like minecraft you can sort  of dig into the hills or you know go  straight down and just build these  teleporters wherever and try to hide  them as best you can and its really  interesting tactic to sort of flank  around the enemy build a spawn point  behind them and hide it really well and  then you can basically just spawn in  right on their base yeah it's pretty  hard for them to find it at least it was  in my experience but of course there was  one time where I built a sky bridge out  of bricks out to a little floating  island and hit it there and I think once  someone sees that sky bridge they think  what what is going on here mr. they  figured it out pretty easily yeah and  it's interesting jagex the guys from  jagex for telling us actually that  they've sort of taken a radical  dedication approach to  just freedom and building and that they  almost didn't allow sky bridging but  they figured that it it'd be more  interesting to just let people have  creative freedom build sky bridges build  platforms that go out forever build as  far out as you can on the map and then  build a straight lain down to the  enemy's base so they're there really is  a radical amount of creative freedom in  this game which is interesting yeah and  you know I'm not necessarily a big fan  of Minecraft but pairing it with a sort  of team-based competitive shooter game I  think that it it helps you know sort of  give it more more legs in a sense the  building and harvesting yeah I am NOT a  Minecraft fan either but it was  interesting for me to have sort of the  the Lego creative approach to a game  like this but with the motivation of  another team competing against you  shooting each other and sort of a MOBA  style base capture mode yeah so if you  are a fan of team fortress 2 and  certainly minecraft keep an eye on block  and load it's going to be coming out  this April in 2015 from jagex on PC  you
 

